      "problem": "Calculate $-81\\div (-9).$",
      "worked_solution": "We have to divide a negative number ${\\color{red}(-81)}$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-9)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14147219/assets/07bfe8691a2be4225626c57bb0fafc4c72801cdd48dd0d7e2ba96538db37a00a.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $81$ by $9$ without any signs: $81 \\div 9 = 9.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-81)} \\div {\\color{red}(-9)} = {\\color{blue}9}.\n$$",
